counterfactuals.output:
1. A video encoding device comprising:

a prediction parameter determination circuit configured to determine, for a current block of a picture to be encoded, a predicted quantization parameter based on at least one of a quantization parameter of a left neighboring block, a quantization parameter of an upper neighboring block, and a quantization parameter used for a previously encoded block;

a quantization parameter generation circuit configured to generate a quantization parameter for the current block using the predicted quantization parameter;

a motion vector predictor selection circuit configured to select, from a plurality of candidate motion vector predictors, a motion vector predictor for the current block;

a motion compensation circuit configured to generate a prediction block for the current block using motion compensation based on the selected motion vector predictor;

a residual generation circuit configured to generate a residual block based on a difference between the current block and the prediction block;

a transform and quantization circuit configured to transform the residual block to generate transform coefficients and to quantize the transform coefficients according to the quantization parameter to generate quantized transform coefficients;

a coefficient scanning circuit configured to scan the quantized transform coefficients according to a scan order, wherein the quantized transform coefficients are divided into a plurality of coefficient subsets and an identical scan pattern is applied to each of the plurality of coefficient subsets; and

an entropy coding circuit configured to entropy-code information including the selected motion vector predictor, information indicating the quantization parameter, and the scanned quantized transform coefficients to generate an encoded video bitstream.

An apparatus for video coding, comprising:

a memory configured to store video data; and

one or more processors coupled to the memory and configured to:

generate, for a current block of a video picture, a prediction block;

generate a residual block based on a difference between the current block and the prediction block;

transform the residual block to generate transform coefficients;

determine a quantization parameter for quantizing the transform coefficients by deriving an averaged quantization parameter from one or more available quantization parameters selected according to a priority order comprising a left-neighbor quantization parameter, an upper-neighbor quantization parameter, and a previous-block quantization parameter;

quantize the transform coefficients using the averaged quantization parameter to generate quantized transform coefficients;

entropy-code the quantized transform coefficients according to a scan pattern;

encode one or more motion vectors associated with the current block using a motion-vector predictor; and

apply the same scan pattern to each of a plurality of coefficient subsets of the quantized transform coefficients.
